1:["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-shell","children":[["$","header",null,{"className":"blog-header","children":[["$","a",null,{"href":"/","className":"wordmark","aria-label":"Wen Reloz, home","children":["wr",["$","span",null,{"children":"."}]]}],["$","nav",null,{"aria-label":"Primary navigation","children":[["$","a",null,{"href":"/","children":"PORTFOLIO"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"/"}],["$","a",null,{"href":"/blog","children":"BLOG"}]]}]]}],["$","main",null,{"className":"article-shell","children":[["$","a",null,{"href":"/blog","className":"back-link","children":[["$","$Ld",null,{"ref":"$undefined","iconNode":[["path",{"d":"m12 19-7-7 7-7","key":"1l729n"}],["path",{"d":"M19 12H5","key":"x3x0zl"}]],"className":"lucide-arrow-left","size":15}]," All articles"]}],["$","article",null,{"children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"eyebrow","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"short-rule"}]," ","NATURE / SOUTHERN LEYTE"]}],["$","h1",null,{"children":["Where the Road Meets the Bay: Pintuyan and Padre Burgos",["$","span",null,{"children":"."}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"article-lede","children":"A slow journey around Sogod Bay, where green roads, quiet coastal towns, and an immense blue horizon meet."}],["$","figure",null,{"className":"article-image","children":[["$","img",null,{"src":"/blog/sogod-story.jpg","alt":"Sunrise reflected across the calm water of Sogod Bay in Southern Leyte"}],["$","figcaption",null,{"children":["Sogod Bay in the quiet light of morning."," ",["$","a",null,{"href":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bontoc_Southern_Leyte.jpg","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer","children":["Photo: ","dbgg1979 · CC BY 2.0",["$","$Ld",null,{"ref":"$undefined","iconNode":[["path",{"d":"M7 7h10v10","key":"1tivn9"}],["path",{"d":"M7 17 17 7","key":"1vkiza"}]],"className":"lucide-arrow-up-right","size":12}]]}]]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"article-rule"}],[["$","div","The road around Sogod Bay feels like an introduction written slowly. Mountains rise on one side and the water keeps appearing on the other—sometimes framed by trees, sometimes opening into a wide blue view. The farther I travel, the less interested I become in arriving quickly.",{"children":[["$","p",null,{"children":"The road around Sogod Bay feels like an introduction written slowly. Mountains rise on one side and the water keeps appearing on the other—sometimes framed by trees, sometimes opening into a wide blue view. The farther I travel, the less interested I become in arriving quickly."}],"$undefined"]}],["$","div","In Pintuyan, mornings belong to the sea. Boats head out with trained local guides and spotters, looking for whale sharks that seasonally follow plankton into these waters. An encounter is never guaranteed, and I like that honesty. The waiting sharpens every detail: the sound of the boat, the changing color of the water, and each gesture from a spotter scanning the surface.",{"children":[["$","p",null,{"children":"In Pintuyan, mornings belong to the sea. Boats head out with trained local guides and spotters, looking for whale sharks that seasonally follow plankton into these waters. An encounter is never guaranteed, and I like that honesty. The waiting sharpens every detail: the sound of the boat, the changing color of the water, and each gesture from a spotter scanning the surface."}],"$undefined"]}],["$","div","What stays with me is not a checklist of sightings. It is the scale of the bay and the feeling of being a guest in it. Pintuyan’s community-led interaction program is handled by trained guides and spotters. The approach makes the experience feel rooted in local knowledge rather than staged for visitors.",{"children":[["$","p",null,{"children":"What stays with me is not a checklist of sightings. It is the scale of the bay and the feeling of being a guest in it. Pintuyan’s community-led interaction program is handled by trained guides and spotters. The approach makes the experience feel rooted in local knowledge rather than staged for visitors."}],"$undefined"]}],"$Le","$Lf","$L10"],"$L11"]}],"$L12"]}],"$L13"]}]
e:["$","div","Across the bay in Padre Burgos, the landscape becomes another doorway into the same living water. The municipality has more than thirty dive sites, and its reefs, walls, and marine sanctuaries attract divers and underwater photographers. Even from shore, the clarity suggests how much life continues beyond what I can see.",{"children":[["$","p",null,{"children":"Across the bay in Padre Burgos, the landscape becomes another doorway into the same living water. The municipality has more than thirty dive sites, and its reefs, walls, and marine sanctuaries attract divers and underwater photographers. Even from shore, the clarity suggests how much life continues beyond what I can see."}],"$undefined"]}]
f:["$","div","By late afternoon, the light softens over the water. Fishing boats become silhouettes and the green coastline darkens behind them. This is when Sogod Bay feels most complete to me—not as one attraction, but as a connected place shaped by communities, roads, reefs, weather, and time.",{"children":[["$","p",null,{"children":"By late afternoon, the light softens over the water. Fishing boats become silhouettes and the green coastline darkens behind them. This is when Sogod Bay feels most complete to me—not as one attraction, but as a connected place shaped by communities, roads, reefs, weather, and time."}],"$undefined"]}]
10:["$","div","I leave Pintuyan and Padre Burgos with the kind of calm nature gives without announcing it. The experience is not loud. It settles in gradually, like the coastal road itself, and becomes something I want to return to.",{"children":[["$","p",null,{"children":"I leave Pintuyan and Padre Burgos with the kind of calm nature gives without announcing it. The experience is not loud. It settles in gradually, like the coastal road itself, and becomes something I want to return to."}],"$undefined"]}]
